args:
- description: |
    A comma-separated string of unique agent IDs used to identify the endpoint across integrated systems. Used to retrieve endpoint data based on agent identifiers. Accepts multiple values.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: endpoint_id
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: endpoint_id
- description: |
    A comma-separated string of IP addresses assigned to the endpoint. Used to locate and collect endpoint data based on IP matching. Accepts multiple values.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: endpoint_ip
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: endpoint_ip
- description: |
    A comma-separated string of hostnames associated with the endpoint. Enables retrieval of endpoint data by matching against known hostnames. Accepts multiple values.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: endpoint_hostname
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: endpoint_hostname
- description: |
    Optional. A comma-separated list of integration brand names to limit which integrations are queried. If omitted, the command queries all available integrations. Useful for targeting specific data sources. Optional values are: 'Active Directory Query v2', 'Cylance Protect v2', 'McAfee ePO v2', 'VMware Carbon Black EDR v2', 'ExtraHop v2', 'CrowdstrikeFalcon', 'Cortex Core - IR'.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: brands
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: brands
- description: |
    Optional. When set to `true`, the command outputs detailed, step-by-step results from each integration. When set to `false` (default), only the final, consolidated result is returned. Optional values: True, False.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: verbose
  required: false
  type: boolean
  underlyingargname: verbose
